  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nWe will improve upon the current construction by incorporating a multi-resolution hill-climbing algorithm with simulated annealing. The key limitations of the original SLSQP approach are:\n1. SLSQP converges too quickly to local optima\n2. Pairwise search doesn't adapt well to problem structure\n3. Repair mechanisms potentially break feasible solutions\n\nMost importantly, we'll:\n1. Decompose the problem into resolution layers\n2. Use simulated annealing for global exploration at each layer\n3. Implement a novel dimension-projection based repair\n4. Include A* guided searches for faster basins hopping\n\nThe core rationale is three-fold:\n1. Simulated annealing escapes local optima better than SLSQP\n2. Progressive resolution handles problem scale adaptively\n3. Operator decomposition aligns with correlation structure\n4. Projection simplifies integral enforcement\n\nWe diagnose the bottleneck as the repair function which can produce infeasible solutions during optimization. The proposed repair preserves both bounds and integral by using piecewise linear envelope projection.\n\nMathematical specification:\nVariables: h \u2208 [0,1]^{2n+1} (odd padding required for full correlation)\nObjective: minimize max_{k} (dx * \u2211 h[x] * (1-h[x+k]))\n\nConstraints:\n1. h(x) \u2208 [0,1] \u2200x\n2. \u222bh(x)dx = 1\n3. Vector constraint: sum(h) = n (with dx=2/n)\n\nRepair function R(x) = clip(x + \u03bc, 0,1) where \u03bc solves:\n  \u2211 clip(x + \u03bc, 0,1) = n/2 (exactly)\n\nDimension transformation: map complete graph correlations to tree-like structure\n\nDetailed steps for multi-stage hill climbing:\n\n1. Top-level initialization\nExpand with convex combination: h = (1-\u03b1)*parent1 + \u03b1*parent2\nSet repair range [0,1] and scale to enforce integral\n\n2. Neighbour generation functions:\n- Swap: toggle a random index (0/1)\n- Shift: move a spike by one position (add/remove from integral)\n- Merge: combine adjacent spikes (keep integral)\n- Split: split a broad hump into two (adjust integral)\n\n3. Temperature schedule:\nT(0)=2.0\nT(t)=T\u2080 * exp(-c*s)\nc=0.9 (cooling factor)\ns=progress/iter\n\n4. Evaluation geometry:\nLocal move weight=0.25\nGlobal move weight=0.75\nInitial temperature=10.0\n\n5. Optimal run conditions:\nMax temperature=5.0\nMin temperature=0.5\nMax iters=10000\nRestarts at T=2.0 when progress stall\n\n6. Smooth surrogate objective:\nObjective = -sum(exp(-|h_i - true_val|\u00b2 / \u03c3\u00b2)))\n\nImplementation procedure:\n\n1. Parent handling:\nAlgorithm shape: input parent vector h_parent\n  - Scale by 0.5: h = h_parent/0.5\n  - Project to sum= n (using bisection)\n  - Move to resolution layer\n\n2. Score calculation:\nCompute correlation magnitude: \n  C5 = max_k [ correlation(h,1-h)[k] * dx ]\n  dx = 2/n\n\n3. Repair procedure:\ndef repair(h,n):\n  target = n/2.0\n  # Strange repair using dimensional projection\n  tol = 1e-9\n  def overlap_index(i):\n    return 2*n+1-2*i  # custom indexing to match convolution\n\n...\n\n[Implementation continues with detailed repair steps, neighbor generators, scoring functions, and complete algorithmic structure]",
